# CHAPTER II

## RIGHTS OF WOMEN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

#### Article 5 

Every woman victim of violence has the right:  
a. to be respected for her dignity as a human being;  
b. to obtain protection from family, community, Regional Government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on a protection order from the court;  
c. to physical, psychological and sexual health recovery in accordance with the suffering experienced by Women Victims of Violence;  
d. to special handling related to the confidentiality of Women Victims of Violence;  
e. to assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;  
f. to spiritual guidance services; and  
g. to determine her own decisions.

# CHAPTER III

## AUTHORITY OF THE REGIONAL GOVERNMENT

#### Article 6 

1. The Regional Government has authority in the Protection of Women. 
2. The authority as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:  
a. prevention of violence against women involving parties within the Regional scope;  
h. provision of services for women Victims of violence requiring Regional level coordination; and  
c. strengthening and development of institutions providing women protection services.

# CHAPTER IV

## PLANNING

#### Article 7

The Regent is obliged to integrate policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women into Regional development planning.  

Article8 (1) The integration of policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women in the Region is set forth in planning and budget documents which include:  
a. Regional Long-Term Development Plan;  
b. Regional Medium-Term Development Plan;  
c. Strategic Plan of Regional Government Work Units;  
d. Regional Government Work Plan; and  
e. Work Plan and Budget of Regional Government Work Units.  
2. The preparation of planning and budget documents as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be harmonized between levels and structures of government.  
3. The Agency facilitates the integration of policies, programs, and activities for the Protection of Women into the preparation of planning and budget documents as referred to in paragraph (1).  
4. In carrying out the facilitation as referred to in paragraph (3), the Agency coordinates with the Regional Development Planning Agency of East Kutai Regency.

# CHAPTER V

## IMPLEMENTATION

### Part One

General

#### Article 9 

1. The Regent is obliged to implement policies, programs, and activities for the Protection of Women, to eliminate all forms of discrimination and acts of violence against women in the region.  
2. The implementation as referred to in paragraph (1) is coordinated by the Vice Regent.  
3. The implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women in the region as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by establishing, developing, strengthening, or utilizing institutions in the Region.

## Part Two

Prevention

#### Article 10

Prevention of acts of violence against women as referred to in article 6 paragraph (2) letter a, the Regional Government carries out the following efforts:  
a. conducting counseling and socialization regarding matters relating to violence against women;  
b. conducting socialization on women's rights;  
c. seeking to improve education for women;  
d. opening skills courses for women to support the family's economic needs;  
e. creating employment opportunities for women;  
f. providing counseling to immediately report to local authorities if violence against women occurs;  
g. empowering social community organizations and women's organizations to increase women's knowledge and insight;  
h. establishing Women Protection Complaint Posts; and  
i. forming networks in efforts to prevent violence.

## Part Three

Protection Services for Women Victims of Violence

#### Article 11

1. The provision of Services for Women victims of violence includes, among others:  
a. providing Services and handling as quickly as possible to Women Victims of Violence;  
b. providing convenience, comfort, safety, and free of charge for Women Victims of Violence;  
c. maintaining the confidentiality of Women Victims of Violence; and  
d. guaranteeing justice and legal certainty for Women Victims of Violence.

## Part Four

Institutions

### Paragraph 1

#### Article 12

1. In supporting the implementation of Women Protection, the Regent establishes PPT.  
2. PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) is in the form of:  
a. UPTD PPA;  
b. hospital-based PPT;  
c. sub-district PPT; and  
d. Village/kelurahan PPT.  
3. Further provisions regarding the procedures for establishing PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) are regulated by Regent Regulation.

#### Article 13 

1. PPT Services include:  
a. providing Services and handling as quickly as possible to Women Victims of Violence;  
b. providing convenience, comfort, safety, and free of charge for Women Victims of Violence;  
c. maintaining the confidentiality of Women Victims of Violence; and  
d. guaranteeing justice and legal certainty for Women Victims of Violence.  
2. Further provisions regarding the procedures for PPT Services as referred to in paragraph (1) are regulated by Regent Regulation.

#### Article 14 

The operation of PPT requires:  
a. adequate supporting facilities and infrastructure;  
b. implementing officers; and  
c. functional officers.

#### Article 15

1. The procedures and mechanisms for integrated Services include:  
a. complaint services;  
b. Health Rehabilitation;  
c. Social Rehabilitation;  
d. Repatriation;  
e. Social Reintegration, and  
f. Legal Aid.  
2. The implementation of integrated services as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out in accordance with SPM.

## Part Five

#### Article 16

1. SPM in the field of integrated services for women and children victims of violence aims to ensure that Women Victims of violence receive the minimum services needed.  
2. SPM in the field of integrated services for Women Victims of violence includes services for:  
a. handling complaints/reports of Victims of Violence Against Women;  
b. health services for women Victims of violence;  
c. social rehabilitation for women Victims of violence;  
d. law enforcement and Legal Aid for women Victims of violence;  
e. Repatriation and Social Reintegration for women Victims of violence; and  
f. in the event that Women Victims of Violence experience trauma or illness that endangers themselves as a result of acts of violence requiring immediate assistance, the Regional Government is obliged to provide first aid no later than 7 (seven) days after the complaint is filed.

#### Article 17 

SPM as referred to in Article 16 has women performance including:  
a. coverage of women victims of violence who receive complaint handling by trained officers in integrated Service units;  
b. coverage of Women Victims of violence who receive indicator services by trained indicator personnel at health centers and hospitals;  
c. coverage of Social Rehabilitation services provided by trained Social Rehabilitation officers for indicator Victims of violence in integrated Service units;  
d. coverage of indicator guidance services provided by trained indicator guidance officers for Women Victims of Violence in integrated Service units;  
e. coverage of law enforcement from the investigation level to court decisions on cases of Violence Against Women;  
f. coverage of Women Victims of Violence who receive Legal Aid services;  
g. coverage of Repatriation services for Women Victims of Violence; and  
h. coverage of Social Reintegration services for Women Victims of Violence.  
2. The determination of SPM performance indicators in the field of integrated services for Women Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) is the minimum target that must be achieved by integrated service units in stages.

## Part Six

Social Protection House
